{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 4.5% a year from $70.3 billion in FY2016 to $104.8 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F205], but the path was a step change, not a smooth climb."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue jumped 19.8% in FY2020 and 13.3% in FY2021 [D183][D230], then fell 1.6%, 0.8% and 1.7% in FY2023 through FY2025 [D324][D370][D416]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 surge came from a 19.3% comparable sales increase and new stores, with the pandemic shifting channel and category mix [P51][P55]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2022 collapse in operating income, down 57.0% [D279], followed discretionary category sales declines and markdowns taken to clear excess inventory [P38]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The window reads as a pandemic pull-forward followed by three years of give-back, leaving revenue below its FY2022 peak [F7][F10]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Food & beverage grew from 19.6% of revenue in FY2017 to 23.0% in FY2025 [D484][D506], contributing 0.3pp in FY2025 [D508]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Apparel & accessories fell 4.7% in FY2025, a 0.7pp drag [D564][D565], and home furnishings & décor declined to $15.6 billion from $20.3 billion in FY2021 [S33][S29]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 comparable sales fell 2.6% on a 2.2% traffic decline and a 0.4% lower average transaction [P14]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income fell 8.1% in FY2025 against a 1.7% revenue decline [D417][D416], so there was no operating leverage."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS compounded at 6.3% versus net income at 3.4% [F210][F208], as diluted shares fell from 582.5 million to 455.6 million [X107][X116]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin was 4.9% in FY2025 [F34], below the 5.6% window median [D590] and far under the 8.4% FY2021 high [D589]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 margin slipped 0.3pp [D429], with cost of revenue taking 0.3pp and SG&A adding 0.1pp [D440][D441]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Gross margin fell to 27.9% from 28.2% [P12], and the SG&A rate held at 20.6% only because of a 0.6pp interchange settlement benefit [P11]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The largest move was FY2022, when operating margin fell 4.9pp [D290] as cost of revenue took 4.6pp [D301] on markdowns and elevated inventory costs [P38]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin of 3.5% [F54] sits 1.4pp under operating margin [F34], with the 22.3% tax rate [D403] and $445 million interest expense [X66] the main gaps."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $6.6 billion was 1.77x net income in FY2025 [F84][D404], and free cash flow of $2.8 billion was 0.77x [F104][D405], under the 1.01x window median [D599]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 operating cash decline reflected lower net earnings and lower accounts payable leverage [P7]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin was 2.7% [D401], below the 4.5% median [D596] and the 4.2% peer median [D611]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex of $3.7 billion was 3.6% of revenue and 1.19x D&A [F94][D400][D406], up 28.9% on new stores and remodels [D423][P5]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net debt was $4.3 billion, or 4.1% of revenue [D410][D411], against a peer median net cash of -3.5% of revenue (n=6) [D613]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cash and investments rose to $10.1 billion [D408] while total debt reached $14.4 billion [D409], and the current ratio held at 0.94x [F184]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $2.5 billion were 86.8% of free cash flow [D412][D413], and the diluted share count fell 1.3% [D434]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Payout above free cash flow in most years has been funded from the cash pile rather than new leverage, which keeps the balance sheet adequate but not strong."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue has declined three straight years, FY2023 through FY2025 [F8][F9][F10][R1], the most persistent issue in the pack."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 drop traces to a 2.6% comparable sales decline on lower traffic [P14], so the trend is demand-led, not store-count-led."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The current ratio of 0.94x [F184][R2] is at the window median [D602], so it reflects normal retail working-capital structure rather than distress."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The 2.4 years of burn coverage [D276][R3] dates from FY2022 and no longer applies, since free cash flow has been positive since [F102][F103][F104]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "FY2022 buybacks and FY2017 SG&A were later restated [R5][R6], so those two figures carry a data-quality caveat."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether operating margin holds above the 4.9% FY2025 level [F34] or falls toward the 3.5% FY2022 low [D588], reported in the FY2026 10-K."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether free cash flow margin recovers toward the 4.5% median [D596] from 2.7% [D401], given guided FY2026 capex of about $5 billion [P4]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether revenue stops declining after three down years [F8][F9][F10], with comparable sales the line to watch in the FY2026 filing [P14]."}
  ]}
]}
